#====================================================================
# Draft: CMake FindCurses has no sysroot notion - it finds the archive
#        but contributes no include dir, so `#include <ncurses.h>`
#        fails to compile in a Conan cross build
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-12002-CMAKE-FINDCURSES-NO-INCLUDE-DIR-SYSCROSS
trigger_tool:           cmake
phase:                  configuration|compilation
error_signature:        Could NOT find Curses \(missing: CURSES_LIBRARY\)|fatal error: 'ncurses.h' file not found|Found Curses: .*libncurses

severity:               2
category:               cmake, cross-compile, ncurses, dependency
match_keywords:         find_package(Curses), FindCurses, CURSES_NEED_NCURSES, link_libraries, CURSES_LIBRARIES, ncurses CONFIG, ncurses::ncurses, cross compile

title:                  find_package(Curses REQUIRED) cannot be satisfied by a conan ncurses package in a cross build: with CURSES_NEED_NCURSES the module reports "Could NOT find Curses (missing: CURSES_LIBRARY)", and once the recipe hands it the archive via the CURSES_LIBRARY cache variable, `link_libraries(${CURSES_LIBRARIES})` contributes that archive alone - no include directory - so the first `#include <ncurses.h>` fails to compile.

root_cause:             CMake's FindCurses module searches library paths without any sysroot notion, so in a cross build (CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME=Linux plus an OHOS clang from the profile conf) it never sees the target's ncurses. Seeding CURSES_LIBRARY/CURSES_NCURSES_LIBRARY makes the find succeed, but ${CURSES_LIBRARIES} expands to a bare path: link_libraries() propagates link flags, not include directories, and upstream projects that use it therefore get "fatal error: 'ncurses.h' file not found". Resolving the dependency through the CONFIG package that Conan generates (ncurses::ncurses) carries the include dir, the static libncursesw.a and the link order in one target.

affected_scope:         Any upstream CMake project using find_package(Curses REQUIRED) + link_libraries(${CURSES_LIBRARIES}) against a conan ncurses package: tmatrix 1.4 (verified), and by the same shape any other terminal application packaged here. Note cmatrix 2.0 solves the related detection problem by symlinking libncurses.a -> libncursesw.a; that is a different symptom (AC_CHECK_LIB) of the same module.

verification_cmd:       grep -n "CURSES" CMakeLists.txt   # after the patch: no CURSES_* should remain

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           use-conan-ncurses-config-target
rec_description:        Replace `find_package(Curses REQUIRED)` + `link_libraries(${CURSES_LIBRARIES})` with `find_package(ncurses CONFIG REQUIRED)` + `link_libraries(ncurses::ncurses)`. Generate the target with CMakeDeps; the ncurses recipe sets cmake_file_name=ncurses / cmake_target_name=ncurses::ncurses, so the CONFIG file is produced automatically. Drop the CURSES_* cache variables entirely - they are not needed once the CONFIG target resolves, and leaving them in produces a "Manually-specified variables were not used by the project" warning.
rec_command:            python3 scripts/ohc-run.py refresh-patch --auto <name> <ver>   # after editing CMakeLists.txt in the work tree
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               archives/t/tmatrix/1.4/patches/0001-CMakeLists.txt.patch

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:       seed-both-variables-and-add-include-directories
fallback_description:   If the CONFIG target is unavailable, keep find_package(Curses) but supply CURSES_INCLUDE_PATH plus CURSES_NCURSES_LIBRARY AND replace link_libraries(${CURSES_LIBRARIES}) with an explicit target_include_directories()/include_directories() for the same path; this is what makes the difference between "found" and "compiles".
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       -D__OHOS__.*CURSES|link_libraries\(\$\{CURSES_LIBRARIES\}\).*#.*as-is
forbid_1_reason:        Platform macros in patches are PF5-blocked; the fix is generic cross-compilation hygiene and needs no platform conditional. Keeping link_libraries(${CURSES_LIBRARIES}) unchanged is the actual bug.
forbid_1_consequence:   Preflight PF5 hard block; or a build that configures cleanly and then fails on the first #include.

principles:             resolve-dependencies-through-their-exported-target, verify-compile-not-just-configure
